  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The ionic character in a molecule is dependent upon the electronegativity difference between the constituting atoms. The greater the difference, the greater will be the ionic character of the molecule.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>LiF</mi></math></p><p>The Ionic character depends upon the difference in electronegativity (bond polarity).</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is a covalent molecule &amp; the difference in electrongegativities are:<br/>|X<sub>S</sub> – X<sub>0</sub>| <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br/>|X<sub>Cl</sub> – X<sub>F</sub>| <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br/>|X<sub>K</sub> – X<sub>0</sub>| <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br/>|X<sub>Li</sub> – X<sub>F</sub>| <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>"
